Fillets: a rounding that vanishes at the end of its spine, where its faces
come tangent, ends where its contact crosses onto a face tangent to the
other face along an edge into that vertex (mitcad#343).

The case: a chain of edges round a band's rim with a large torus F14, its
last edge between F14 and an earlier rounding D, ending at a vertex V where
D runs on tangentially across an edge into a rounding C of F14 (C tangent
to F14 along an edge into V): D, C and F14 are all tangent at V, the
rounding vanishes there. The walk's contact on D crossed onto C a hundredth
of the radius before V; between C and F14, tangent along their edge, no
ball fits, and the next piece's walk failed, which failed the whole
stripe. On another body, a few micrometres off, the stripe ended there but
the end, 0.011 from V, was not put at V (ChFi3d_ShrinkVanishingEnd takes
ends within a hundredth of the radius whose faces' normals are within
0.002 rad; here 0.006 at the contacts), and the OnSame corner that took
it crashed: the cap's p-curve on the face at the end was not found and
ChFi3d_ComputeArete used it.

- ChFi3d_ContactOntoTangentFaceAtEnd: whether a piece's end has one
  contact on an edge E of its face F that runs to the spine's end vertex V,
  the face beyond E tangent to F along E and to the blend's other face
  along an edge from V, both contacts within two hundredths of the radius
  of V and within a hundredth of each other.
- PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine: at a tangency extremity such a piece ends the
  stripe, as one whose contacts reached V (0400).
- PerformFilletOnVertex: such an end is put at V (the blend ends in a
  point there, PerformSingularCorner) within two hundredths of the radius,
  its faces' normals not compared: they are tangent at V, the walk only
  could not get nearer.
- ChFi3d_ComputeArete returns without a p-curve where its projection
  fails (the callers find none and fail), instead of using it.

Upstream: new.

